# Ship flow

Product work starts and finishes from a Cursor agent request. Full procedure: `.cursor/skills/ship-gate/SKILL.md`.

EASM ships two ways:

- **Shelters self-host**: download/clone, Composer, `/install` (README). Agents never push to shelter hosting.
- **APES Cloudron instance**: the only deploy target. Cloudron app id is repo variable `CLOUDRON_APP_ID` (`7afd5173-8880-4e64-9c36-5f978d9c8f64`, `easm.intranet.apes.org.uk`). Deploy runs through `.github/workflows/deploy-cloudron.yml`, triggered by publishing a GitHub Release.

## Track work in GitHub while working

1. On start: find or create the leaf issue (and sub-issues when work splits), set its milestone, assignee `apescic-director`, `area:` labels; branch `cursor/{feature|fix|chore}/<n>-<slug>`.
2. While working: comment progress, decisions and blockers on the issue; tick acceptance criteria; open sub-issues and link them to the parent.
3. On finish: close the leaf issue via the PR (`Fixes #<n>`), comment the outcome, close parents/epics only when every child is closed, and close the milestone when it has no open issues.

## Autonomous ship (default)

Once the slice is complete, run the whole sequence without stopping, **as long as every check is green**:

1. **Verify** (Laragon PHP via `scripts/local/use-laragon.ps1`): `composer test` exits 0; `composer lint` once (at most one `composer format`, then re-lint once); UI smoke on `http://easm.test` when HTTP/views/routes changed. Docker build when `Dockerfile`, `cloudron/` or `CloudronManifest.json` changed.
2. **Commit** on the `cursor/...` branch (no secrets, no `.env`), push with `-u`.
3. **PR** with `Fixes #<n>`; wait for CI (`gh pr checks --watch`).
4. **Merge** (`gh pr merge --merge --delete-branch`) and confirm the merge commit on `main`.
5. **Release**: patch bump (`vX.Y.Z+1`) per merged PR; minor bump (`vX.Y+1.0`) when the PR closes the last open issue in a milestone. Update `APP_VERSION` in `.env.example` and the fallback in `config/app.php` in the PR before merge.
6. **Deploy**: publishing the release triggers `Deploy to Cloudron`; watch it and confirm `https://easm.intranet.apes.org.uk/health` reports the new version.

## Stop and offer options

Stop (no commit, merge, release or deploy beyond that point) when any of these happen:

- a test, lint, smoke, CI, release or deploy step fails;
- Cloudron secrets are missing or the deploy needs `first_deploy=true`;
- the version bump, scope or a product decision is unclear;
- the work would touch shelter hosting, secrets, or another repo.

Whenever stopping or when the user must choose, end the turn with:

```markdown
## Next actions
**Recommended:** <one option and why>

1. ...
2. ...
3. ...
```

Even when nothing is blocked, finish with the same menu of best next options (for example the next issue in the implement order).

## Completion

After deploy is verified: report PR link, short merge SHA, target branch, release URL, deploy run URL plus `/health` version, and the issues/milestone closed. Offer to archive the agent; never archive silently.
